/-!
# Path independence for matching choice

`ChoiceFunction.PathIndependent` is the general path-independence condition
on menus. In matching with contracts, the same condition applies with
contracts as alternatives.

This topic entrypoint imports the canonical definition and its union
identities from `MathEconLib.Choice.Conditions.General.PathIndependence`.
The equivalence with substitutability and irrelevance of rejected contracts
is proved in `MathEconLib.Choice.Conditions.General.Relationships`.
It introduces no separate matching predicate.
-/
